{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Working Hard", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Meeting the Editor", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B2.2", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": " Analyze issues relating to different topics and their solution in written and spoken situations according to work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": " Integrates a wider range of written and spoken language skills and knowledge when dealing with problems and difficulties in the workplace.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": " Understands the main ideas and specific information of complex text on both concrete and abstract topics in written texts in social and work contexts.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to take precedence", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be \u200bconsidered more \u200bimportant than other things", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Let's have a look at what needs to take precedence.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to talk about work responsibilities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "consistency", "type": "name"}, {"content": " the \u200bquality of always \u200bhappening in a \u200bsimilar way", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Errors in grammar, spelling and consistency need to be identified.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "manuscript ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the \u200boriginal \u200bcopy of a \u200bbook or \u200barticle before it is \u200bprinted", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We have two chapters of a manuscript that need to be edited.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "in-house", "type": "name"}, {"content": "work done within a company rather than by outside contractors", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  I'll just remind you that our in-house style guidelines need to be followed. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "liberty", "type": "name"}, {"content": "freedom", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: At this stage you have the liberty to rewrite.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to see fit ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to think is necessary", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Make changes as you see fit.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to scrutinize ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to check carefully", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I will focus my attention on scrutinizing the texts. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "layout", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the way that something is \u200barranged", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We also have some layout that you can do.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob02aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "caption", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a \u200bshort description or explanation below an image ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are you good at writing headlines and captions?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob02aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"content": "engenn10le09ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Need + Passive Infinitive", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You usually use <span class=\"italic\">need </span>as a normal verb to express necessity. You use the passive infinitive in some constructions using the passive voice.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Subject + Need + Passive Infinitive<br/><br/>  For example:<br/><br/>  <span class=\"italic\">First, we have two chapters of a manuscript that <span class=\"strong\">need to be edited</span>. </span><br/><br/>  The subject of the sentence is the thing that needs to be done (two chapters of a manuscript).<br/><br/>  When you choose to use the passive, you are choosing to shift the focus of the sentence to the receiver of the action, rather than the agent (the doer of the action). It is common to use the passive structure when you want to be more polite or in more formal situations, like the workplace. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We have two chapters of a manuscript that need to be edited.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Our in-house style guidelines need to be followed.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Errors in grammar, spelling and consistency need to be identified.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "These chapters need to be completed by Thursday, end of day.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Checking for errors of fact also needs to be done.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": " Clauses using verb+ing", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You can use clauses with verb+ing in different ways. Remember, a clause is a part of a sentence that has its own subject and verb.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Position\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Example\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" As subject\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">Achieving so much at an early age</span> is wonderful.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" As object\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I love <span class=\\\"strong\\\">listening to music at night</span>.</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" After a preposition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">You need to focus on <span class=\\\"strong\\\">learning a lot in a little amount of time</span>.</span>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "Read the following examples from the dialogue. Notice the position of the clause with verb+ing. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Talking with Rob about the style guide will make it clearer.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Completing that editing will be a priority.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I will focus my attention on scrutinizing the texts. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Using the style guide will make this easy for you.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I plan on developing this skill.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think about work that you need to do at your job, at school or at home.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a list of things that need to be done or need doing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Put them in order of importance or priority from most important to least important.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If possible, go around your classroom and share your to-do list. Ask if any students can help you to do any of your tasks.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a list of things that need to be done.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I put my list in order of importance.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my list with classmates.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I ask for help to do my tasks.", "type": "text"}]}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"_data": [{"type": "lab_options", "contents": [{"content": true, "type": "has_nav"}, {"content": true, "type": "has_exercise_controls"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "img_path": "", "id": 0, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content":